---
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial process"
  description="How PC - the blog uses AI assistance while Paolo Cargnin remains accountable for every published Post."
>
  <SiteHeader slot="header" currentPath={Astro.url.pathname} />
  <article id="top" aria-labelledby="editorial-title">
    <header>
      <p>PUBLICATION RECORD</p>
      <h1 id="editorial-title">Editorial process</h1>
      <p class="deck">Writing is human work. Tools can assist; accountability cannot be delegated.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Accountability</h2>
      <p>
        Paolo Cargnin is the Author of every Post and remains responsible for its argument,
        accuracy, judgment, and publication. A Post is published only after human approval;
        no automated system may publish on its own.
      </p>

      <h2>Where AI can help</h2>
      <p>
        AI may help frame questions, organize research, compare outlines, suggest revisions,
        identify counterarguments, check consistency, and support technical or editorial work.
        It may also help draft or revise language when Paolo judges that assistance useful.
      </p>

      <h2>What still requires human judgment</h2>
      <p>
        AI output is not a source and is treated as material to verify, not as evidence. Paolo
        evaluates factual claims against attributable sources, reviews the final text, and
        decides whether it is fair, useful, and ready to publish. Significant AI contributions
        to a particular Post are disclosed on that Post when readers need that context.
      </p>

      <h2>Verification and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        The reporting, editing, and fact-checking process is proportionate to the claim's risk.
        Private source material and unpublished work stay out of the public repository. If a
        published Post needs a substantive correction, the change is recorded visibly on the
        Post alongside its original publication record.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  article {
    max-width: 70rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 10rem) clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2rem) clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
  }

  header {
    max-width: 58rem;
  }

  header > p:first-child {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--signal);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  h1,
  h2 {
    font-weight: 450;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    line-height: 0.9;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(3.7rem, 9vw, 9.5rem);
  }

  .deck {
    max-width: 48ch;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.9rem + 0.3vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 0.98rem + 0.3vw, 1.28rem);
    line-height: 1.74;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 3em 0 0.7em;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 1.3vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1.65em;
  }
</style>
